# Predator Guard - environment template.
#
# Copy it to apps/web/.env.local: Next only loads env files from the app
# directory, so a .env in the repository root is silently ignored.
#
# The app runs with NO configuration: in development, when no Ring credentials
# are present, simulator mode fills in fake credentials, an HMAC key, a token
# key and base URLs pointing at the bundled fake Ring API (see README).

# ---- Real Ring credentials (from the Ring developer portal) ----
# All of RING_CLIENT_ID / RING_CLIENT_SECRET / RING_HMAC_KEY must be set
# together, or config validation fails loudly. The HMAC key verifies webhook
# signatures (hex) AND mints account-linking nonces (base64url) - same key,
# two encodings.
RING_CLIENT_ID=
RING_CLIENT_SECRET=
RING_HMAC_KEY=

# ---- Fastest path to real Ring: one pasted access token ----
# With RING_ACCESS_TOKEN set, Ring calls use exactly this token: no account
# linking, nothing stored, no refresh - re-paste a fresh one when Ring answers
# 401 (tokens are short-lived). The farm is created from GET /v1/users/me on
# first use. Setting this alone is enough to boot, so the credentials above are
# not required; webhook verification stays disabled (503) until RING_HMAC_KEY
# is set, because a signature nobody can verify is worse than an outage.
# NEVER paste a real value into this file - it is tracked in git, and GitHub
# push protection blocks the push. Real values go in apps/web/.env.local
# (gitignored); the lines below are documentation only.
# RING_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# ---- Optional model keys (vision / LLM fallbacks) ----
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ---- Animal identification (F5, OpenCode - one call per capture) ----
# Ring already says "animal"; this key tells the owner WHAT animal.
# Put the real key ONLY in apps/web/.env.local (gitignored), never here.
# Unset => no API call is made and captures stay "Identification pending".
# OPENCODE_API_KEY=
# OPENCODE_VISION_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5
# OPENCODE_BASE_URL=https://opencode.ai/zen/v1

# ---- Token vault ----
# 32 bytes as 64 hex characters (openssl rand -hex 32) or Base64.
# Required outside simulator mode; tokens are sealed with AES-256-GCM.
TOKEN_ENC_KEY=

# ---- Mode switch (no code fork between fake and real Ring) ----
# RING_SIM=1 forces the simulator even when credentials are set.
# Unset with no credentials in development => simulator automatically.
# RING_SIM=
# RING_API_BASE_URL=https://api.amazonvision.com
# RING_OAUTH_BASE_URL=https://oauth.ring.com

# ---- Database ----
# Postgres connection string. Omitted (or empty) => embedded PGlite.
# docker compose up -d db  provides one locally.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://predator_guard:predator_guard@localhost:5432/predator_guard
# Where PGlite keeps its data directory (default: .pglite, gitignored).
# PGLITE_DATA_DIR=
